# Two Vercel apps (do not mix)

| URL | Project | Tree | What it is |
|---|---|---|---|
| **https://ngmi-stage.vercel.app** | `ngmi-stage` (`prj_CAYYd91QDAJvDJSwLDPWnGN5gfRb`) | `/tmp/ngmi-stage` + `apps/web` | Next.js tote. Title **NGMI staging**. |
| **https://ngmi.markets** | `ngmi` (`prj_RVPkHN5tGZFTCrte7DMZMMrkiMp0`) | `apps/landing` | Static splash. Title **NGMI — over the mark before T**. |

If `ngmi-stage.vercel.app` title is the splash line, landing overwrote it. Redeploy the tote immediately. Never `vercel --name ngmi-stage` from `apps/landing`. Never `vercel link` landing to `ngmi-stage`. Never set this project's root to `apps/landing`. `git.deploymentEnabled` is false on the tote.

## Tote deploy

After any `apps/web` change, deploy **ngmi-stage** before saying the work is done. `apps/web` stays gitignored.

Sync into `/tmp/ngmi-stage` (keep `.vercel` and `.env.local`). Workspace yaml in that tree **must** include `apps/web`. Root directory `apps/web`, framework `nextjs`. Then:

```
npx --yes vercel@latest deploy --prod --yes --cwd /tmp/ngmi-stage --scope frsr --logs
```

Splash deploys: `pnpm deploy` inside `apps/landing` only (asserts project `ngmi`).
